cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize this reflection-free columnar serialization engine in your academic systems research or production data planes, please cite it using these metadata."
authors:
  - given-names: "Eklavya"
    family-names: "Saini"
    website: "https://github.com"
title: "Sliver: A Zero-Allocation, Reflection-Free Columnar Storage and Packing Primitive Outside the Go Heap"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
url: "https://github.com/Sliver"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sliver"
abstract: >-
  Sliver is an extreme-throughput, zero-allocation schema-free columnar serialization 
  and memory-packing engine written in pure Go. By completely bypassing the Go runtime heap 
  via native system call allocations and organizing data into layout-stable columnar vectors, 
  Sliver enables high-frequency record encoding, filtering, and retrieval via direct, 
  reflection-free unsafe pointer offset calculations, eliminating Garbage Collection scanning 
  overhead and CPU cache fragmentation at bare-metal memory speeds.
keywords:
  - golang
  - serialization
  - columnar-storage
  - zero-copy
  - lock-free
  - off-heap
  - zero-allocation
  - systems-programming
